Instead, we can use the fact that a strictly increasing subsequence must have at least one element that is greater than all the previous elements. We can use a sliding window of size 2 to find such an element. If we find an element that is greater than all the previous elements, we can add it to the current window and shift all the previous elements one position to the right. If we cannot find such an element, we know that the current window is the longest increasing subsequence, and we can return its length.

